nequality\n  \\[\n  k\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{k+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor\\ge\\frac{k(k+1)}2\n  \\]\n  holds only when \\(k\\) is odd.\n\n* The cases \\(k=2\\) and \\(k=3\\) are impossible for every \\(n\\): the set \\(S_2\\) consists of three points any two of which determine a line parallel to one of the forbidden directions, and the set \\(S_3\\) cannot be partitioned into three sunny lines (a short case‑by‑case verification shows this).\n\nThese results leave the problem of deciding, for each odd \\(k\\ge5\\), whether \\(S_k\\) can be covered by \\(k\\) sunny lines.  The answer to that sub‑problem would complete the description of all admissible \\(k\\) for general \\(n\\).  I was not able to settle this sub‑problem, and therefore cannot give the full list of admissible values of \\(k\\) for arbitrary \\(n\\).\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
